## Paper Corrections ([ieee_paper.tex](file:///Users/namangarg/Desktop/Gaurav%20Verma/ieee_paper.tex))

### Numbers Updated

| Where | Old | New |
|-------|-----|-----|
| Abstract MSE | 82.17 | **76.42** |
| Abstract RMSE/MAE | missing | **8.74 / 6.85** |
| Optimal epoch | 7th (stopped 12) | **5th (stopped 10)** |
| SOTA table RMSE/MAE | 9.06 / 8.34 | **8.74 / 6.85** |
| Ablation baseline | 82.17 | **76.42** |
| Ablation deltas | +146%, +43%, +78% | **+346%, +160%, +100%** |

### False Claims Removed

| Claim | Issue | Fix |
|-------|-------|-----|
| "order-4 Chebyshev Bandpass [0.5, 8.0 Hz]" | **No filter exists in code** — only Z-score normalization | Removed, replaced with accurate description |
| "Q/K/V multi-head attention" equation | Code uses **learnable-query dot-product**, not Q/K/V | Rewrote equation, pseudocode, and all references |
| "2D ResNet CNN" | Code is plain **3-layer Conv2D** | Fixed in TikZ diagram |
| "multi-headed Cross-Attention" | Single learnable query vector | Changed to "learnable-query" |
| "mathematically guarantees" | Overstated | Softened to "enables" |
| Pseudoscience section | "Information Entropy and Topological Mapping" | **Removed entirely** |
| Dropout(0.4) | Code uses 0.3 | **Fixed to 0.3** |

### Limitations Expanded

Added two new critical limitations:
1. **Glucose range disparity** — Validation set only covers 88–136 mg/dL vs training's 88–183 mg/dL, meaning 100% Zone A may not generalize to hyperglycemia
2. **Attention weight imbalance** — 2D branch gets ~100% weight; 1D/3D branches contribute negligibly

